renderObjectList: filter registry entries by class or ID and optional runtime classes; show visible/total count, stable class/ID order, empty state and keyboard-accessible Open actions; preserve object-button focus across refresh.
selectInspectorSection: show the selected Interface/Methods/State/Workspace panel and relevant results; update tab selection and keyboard focus order.
prepareInspectorSections: choose Interface when available, Methods otherwise, or preserve a valid prior section on refresh.
filterInspectorMethods: filter selector buttons without changing their order or invocation.
Support arrow/Home/End tab selection and wrap keyboard focus within the object dialog. Refresh registry periodically.

Process objects are public shell jobs and remain visible when Runtime objects is disabled. Present public builtin names such as Process, Array and Dictionary without internal underscores, and sort/filter using those friendly names.
